  "result": "Excellent! The bulk discount implementation is complete and all 386 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Bulk Discount Feature\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Added bulk discount logic to `lineDiscount()` in `src/totals.js`\n- Bulk discount: 2.5% off lines with qty \u2265 10\n- Applied AFTER the line's own discount (or tier discount) to the remaining amount\n- VAT is calculated on the amount after both discounts\n\n**How it works:**\nFor a line with qty \u2265 10:\n1. Calculate line discount (explicit or tier): `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`\n2. Calculate bulk discount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 2.5 / 100`\n3. Total discount = line discount + bulk discount\n4. VAT is calculated on: `lineTotal - totalDiscount`\n\n**Example:**\n- 10 units \u00d7 \u20ac100 = \u20ac1000\n- No line discount: \u20ac0\n- Bulk discount (2.5%): \u20ac1000 \u00d7 2.5% = \u20ac25\n- Amount for VAT: \u20ac975\n- VAT (21%): \u20ac975 \u00d7 21% = \u20ac205\n- **Total: \u20ac1000 - \u20ac25 + \u20ac205 = \u20ac1,180**\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- 40+ new tests in `test/totals.test.js` covering:\n  - Bulk discount validation\n  - Discount with various line/tier discounts\n  - VAT calculations with bulk discount\n  - Complex multi-line scenarios with mixed conditions\n- Updated existing tests in both test files to reflect the new behavior",
